    "content": "Somali President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud attended the opening of the 81st session of the United Nations General Assembly on 22 September 2026 at the UN headquarters in New York, United States. The annual gathering brings together world leaders to discuss global issues.\n\nDuring the session, President Mohamud is scheduled to address the assembly, presenting Somalia's advancements in state-building, democratization, security, economic growth, and social service delivery. He will also outline Somalia's priorities and the government's efforts to strengthen peace, security, and international cooperation.\n\nThis marks another appearance by the Somali president at the UNGA, reflecting Somalia's ongoing engagement with the international community. In recent years, Somalia has made strides in rebuilding its institutions and combating militant groups, though challenges remain.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the president's participation signals continued international attention to Somalia's development and stability. Many diaspora members closely follow such events, as they often influence remittances, investment opportunities, and the country's global standing.\n\nThe president's address is expected to reaffirm Somalia's commitment to multilateral cooperation and highlight the importance of sustained international support for its recovery and peacebuilding efforts.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/22/madaxweyne-xasan-sheekh-oo-ka-qayb-galay-furitaanka-meertada-81-aad-ee-golaha-guud-ee-qaramada-midoobay/",
