    "content": "Somalia's Minister of Defense, Ahmed Moallim Fiqi, met with a high-level delegation from the Pakistan Air Force in Mogadishu on Monday. The delegation was led by Air Marshal Muhammad Sarfraz, the Air Force Commander and Vice Chief of the Air Staff of Pakistan. Also present at the meeting was the Commander of the Somali Air Force, Brigadier General Abdirahman Mohamud Haji.\n\nThe discussions centered on strengthening defense cooperation between Somalia and Pakistan, with a particular emphasis on the reconstruction and capacity building of the Somali Air Force. Both sides exchanged views on mutual interests and regional security issues.\n\nThis meeting is part of Somalia's ongoing efforts to rebuild its national security forces after decades of conflict. Pakistan has been a partner in training and equipping Somali forces, and this latest engagement signals a continued commitment to that partnership.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, improved security and a stronger national army are crucial for the country's stability and development. Many diaspora members have invested in Somalia and maintain strong ties, and a capable air force is seen as a key component in combating militant groups and securing borders.\n\nThe meeting concluded with both sides reaffirming their commitment to deepening bilateral defense ties. No specific agreements or timelines were announced, but the discussions are expected to lead to further collaboration in military training and technical support.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/22/soomaaliya-iyo-pakistan-oo-xoojinaya-iskaashiga-difaaca-iyo-tayeynta-ciidanka-cirka/",
